+## Receipt-time retained visual reversal (V9)
+
+A new accepted receipt revokes every previous native callback for its known exact
+family before any external context work. If the owned scene has immutable retained
+sources, displayed visual state, a resolved constant new direction, and the same
+family mode, receipt handling queues one provisional renderer retarget immediately.
+The renderer chooses each output's actual presented origin and a shared progress
+clock; the service never substitutes a computed rectangle. This visual continuation
+is not workspace, family, capture or native authority.
+
+The provisional scene is journaled with its new receipt/token before retarget is
+queued. It cannot receive native authority until a fresh consistent context equals
+its retained context and exact fresh family/geometry validation succeeds. Context
+rejection or mismatch cancels the provisional scene without committing the newly
+unvalidated direction. Unknown families, unresolved initial directions and changed
+single-family modes wait for context and fresh relation proof. A failed retarget
+queue is recorded and cannot authorize old callbacks; after fresh validation the
+latest native intent may settle through the ordinary guarded failure path.
+
+Superseded context completions cannot create a second token, enqueue validation,
+or change workspace. A subsequent receipt can reuse the same retained textures
+even while the previous provisional request still waits for context. A successful
+activation starts metadata work on the already reserved scene, preserving its
+token and source provenance. Fresh native replacement/recovery remains separate.
